WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.550
The garbage rules come from an international treaty, MARPOL Annex five.

2
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.550
Plastics first.

3
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:11.000
That includes fishing line, nets and bags.

4
00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:13.825
Where can you put plastic over the side?

5
00:00:14.825 --> 00:00:16.300
Nowhere.

6
00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:19.150
Never, at any distance from land.

7
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.900
Food waste is the only thing with a distance attached.

8
00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:27.150
If it’s ground up, three nautical miles or more from land.

9
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.050
If it isn’t ground, twelve nautical miles or more.

10
00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:36.050
Paper, glass, metal and most other garbage don’t go overboard at all.

11
00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.000
Bring them ashore.

12
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:42.800
And inside three miles, or on inland waters, nothing goes over.

13
00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:46.000
Here’s the simple version for a charter boat.

14
00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:48.600
Bring everything back to the dock.

15
00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:54.400
Put a trash can where your customers can see it, and tell them about it in your safety briefing.
